## **Manage Items Section Implementation**

I've successfully created a complete "Manage Items" section in the dashboard that has the same functionality as the customer section. Here's what was implemented:

### **1. HTML Structure Added to dashboard.html**

<augment_code_snippet path="pahana-edu-back-end/src/main/webapp/dashboard.html" mode="EXCERPT">
```html
<!-- Manage Items Section -->
<div class="manage-items" style="display: none;">
 <h2>Manage Items</h2>
 <form id="itemForm">
 <div class="form-grid">
 <div class="form-floating">
 <input type="text" class="form-control" id="itemName" placeholder="Item Name" aria-label="Item Name" required pattern="[A-Za-z0-9\s]{2,}">
 <label for="itemName">Item Name</label>
 </div>
 <div class="form-floating">
 <input type="number" class="form-control" id="itemPrice" placeholder="Price" aria-label="Price" required min="0" step="0.01">
 <label for="itemPrice">Price ($)</label>
 </div>
 <div class="form-floating">
 <input type="number" class="form-control" id="itemQuantity" placeholder="Quantity" aria-label="Quantity" required min="0">
 <label for="itemQuantity">Quantity</label>
 </div>
 </div>
 <button class="btn btn-primary" type="button" id="btnAddItem">
 <span class="spinner-border spinner-border-sm" role="status" aria-hidden="true" style="display: none;"></span>
 Add Item
 </button>
 </form>
 <div class="table-responsive">
 <table class="table table-striped">
 <thead>
 <tr>
 <th data-sort="id">ID <i class="bi bi-arrow-down-up"></i></th>
 <th data-sort="name">Name <i class="bi bi-arrow-down-up"></i></th>
 <th data-sort="price">Price <i class="bi bi-arrow-down-up"></i></th>
 <th data-sort="quantity">Quantity <i class="bi bi-arrow-down-up"></i></th>
 <th>Actions</th>
 </tr>
 </thead>
 <tbody id="itemTableBody">
 <tr>
 <td colspan="5" class="text-center text-muted">No items added yet.</td>
 </tr>
 </tbody>
 </table>
 </div>
 <!-- Update Item Modal -->
 <div class="modal fade" id="updateItemModal" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="updateItemModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
 <!-- Modal content for updating items -->
 </div>
</div>
```
</augment_code_snippet>

### **2. Navigation Integration**

**Added items navigation logic** to show/hide the items section when users click the "Items" nav:

<augment_code_snippet path="pahana-edu-back-end/src/main/webapp/views/js/Dashboard.js" mode="EXCERPT">
```javascript
// Navigation handling
if (navItem === 'customers') {
 $('.content .manage-customers').show();
 localStorage.setItem('activeNav', 'customers');
 loadAllCustomers();
} else if (navItem === 'items') {
 $('.content .manage-items').show();
 localStorage.setItem('activeNav', 'items');
 loadAllItems(); // Load all items when navigating to items page
} else if (navItem === 'home') {
 $('.content .row.g-4.mb-4').show();
 $('.content .card.mb-4').show();
 $('.content .card').last().show();
 localStorage.setItem('activeNav', 'home');
}
```
</augment_code_snippet>

### **3. Load All Items Functionality**

**Integrated with your existing GetAllItemsServlet** (`/items` endpoint):

<augment_code_snippet path="pahana-edu-back-end/src/main/webapp/views/js/Dashboard.js" mode="EXCERPT">
```javascript
// Function to load all items
function loadAllItems() {
 $.ajax({
 url: 'http://localhost:8080/pahana/items',
 type: 'GET',
 success: function (items) {
 $('#itemTableBody').empty();
 if (items.length === 0) {
 $('#itemTableBody').append('<tr><td colspan="5" class="text-center text-muted">No items found.</td></tr>');
 } else {
 items.forEach(function (item) {
 $('#itemTableBody').append(`
 <tr>
 <td>${item.id}</td>
 <td>${item.name}</td>
 <td>$${item.price.toFixed(2)}</td>
 <td>${item.quantity}</td>
 <td>
