 Implementation Example ===\\n\");\n \n // 1. Factory Pattern Example\n demonstrateFactoryPattern();\n \n // 2. Builder Pattern Example\n demonstrateBuilderPattern();\n \n // 3. Observer Pattern Example\n demonstrateObserverPattern();\n \n // 4. Command Pattern Example\n demonstrateCommandPattern();\n \n // 5. Strategy Pattern Example\n demonstrateStrategyPattern();\n \n System.out.println(\"\\n=== All Design Patterns Demonstrated Successfully ===\");\n }\n \n private static void demonstrateFactoryPattern() {\n System.out.println(\"1. FACTORY PATTERN DEMONSTRATION:\");\n System.out.println(\"Creating DAO instances using DAOFactory...\");\n \n // Using Factory Pattern to get DAO instances\n DAOFactory factory = DAOFactory.getInstance();\n \n System.out.println(\"- CustomerDAO created: \" + (factory.getCustomerDAO() != null));\n System.out.println(\"- ItemDAO created: \" + (factory.getItemDAO() != null));\n System.out.println(\"- BillDAO created: \" + (factory.getBillDAO() != null));\n System.out.println(\"- AdminDAO created: \" + (factory.getAdminDAO() != null));\n \n // Demonstrate singleton behavior\n DAOFactory factory2 = DAOFactory.getInstance();\n System.out.println(\"- Factory singleton working: \" + (factory == factory2));\n System.out.println();\n }\n \n private static void demonstrateBuilderPattern() {\n System.out.println(\"2. BUILDER PATTERN DEMONSTRATION:\");\n System.out.println(\"Creating API responses using Builder Pattern...\");\n \n // Success response with data\n ApiResponse successResponse = new ApiResponse.Builder()\n .success(true)\n .message(\"Operation completed successfully\")\n .data(\"Sample data\")\n .addMetadata(\"timestamp\", System.currentTimeMillis())\n .addMetadata(\"version\", \"1.0\")\n .build();\n \n System.out.println(\"- Success Response: \" + successResponse.toMap());\n \n // Error response\n ApiResponse errorResponse = ApiResponse.error(\"Something went wrong\", 400);\n System.out.println(\"- Error Response: \" + errorResponse.toMap());\n \n // Simple success response\n ApiResponse simpleResponse = ApiResponse.success(\"Task completed\");\n System.out.println(\"- Simple Response: \" + simpleResponse.toMap());\n System.out.println();\n }\n \n private static void demonstrateObserverPattern() {\n System.out.println(\"3. OBSERVER PATTERN DEMONSTRATION:\");\n System.out.println(\"Setting up audit observers and triggering events...\");\n \n AuditManager auditManager = AuditManager.getInstance();\n \n // Add a custom observer\n AuditObserver customObserver = new AuditObserver() {\n @Override\n public void handleEvent(AuditEvent event) {\n System.out.println(\" [CUSTOM OBSERVER] Event: \" + event.getEventType() + \n \" - \" + event.getDescription());\n }\n \n @Override\n public String getObserverName() {\n return \"CustomExampleObserver\";\n }\n };\n \n auditManager.addObserver(customObserver);\n System.out.println(\"- Observers registered: \" + auditManager.getObserverCount());\n \n // Trigger some events\n auditManager.logEvent(AuditEvent.EventType.USER_LOGIN, \"testUser\", \"User logged in\");\n auditManager.logEvent(AuditEvent.EventType.CUSTOMER_CREATED, \"admin\", \"New customer added\");\n \n // Remove custom observer\n auditManager.removeObserver(customObserver);\n System.out.println(\"- Observers after removal: \" + auditManager.getObserverCount());\n System.out.println();\n }\n \n private static void demonstrateCommandPattern() {\n System.out.println(\"4. COMMAND PATTERN DEMONSTRATION:\");\n System.out.println(\"Creating and executing commands...\");\n \n // Create sample bill items\n List<BillItem> billItems = new ArrayList<>();\n BillItem item1 = new BillItem();\n item1.setItemId(1);\n item1.setQuantity(2);\n billItems.add(item1);\n \n // Create command\n CreateBillCommand command = new CreateBillCommand(\"CUST001\", billItems, \"admin\");\n \n System.out.println(\"- Command created: \" + command.getDescription());\n System.out.println(\"- Command can undo: \" + command.canUndo());\n \n // Note: We won't execute this command as it requires database setup\n System.out.println(\"- Command ready for execution (requires database)\");\n System.out.println();\n }\n \n private static void demonstrateStrategyPattern() {\n System.out.println(\"5. STRATEGY PATTERN DEMONSTRATION:\");\n System.out.println(\"Demonstrating different strategies...\");\n \n // Authentication Strategy\n AdminSessionAuthenticationStrategy authStrategy = new AdminSessionAuthenticationStrategy();\n System.out.println(\"- Auth Strategy Error Message: \" + authStrategy.getErrorMessage());\n System.out.println(\"- Auth Strategy Error Code: \" + authStrategy.getErrorStatusCode());\n \n // Response Strategy\n JsonResponseStrategy responseStrategy = new JsonResponseStrategy();\n System.out.println(\"- JSON Response Strategy created successfully\");\n \n System.out.println(\"- Strategies can be swapped at runtime for different behaviors\");\n System.out.println();\n }\n \n /**\n * Example of how to use patterns together in a service method\n */\n public static void integratedExample() {\n System.out.println(\"INTEGRATED EXAMPLE:\");\n System.out.println(\"Using multiple patterns together...\");\n \n try {\n // Factory Pattern - Get service with injected dependencies\n CustomerService customerService = new CustomerService();\n \n // Create a customer\n Customer customer = new Customer();\n customer.setAccountNumber(\"CUST001\");\n customer.setFullName(\"John Doe\");\n customer.setTelephone(\"123-456-7890\");\n customer.setAddress(\"123 Main St\");\n customer.setUnitsConsumed(100);\n \n // Observer Pattern - This will trigger audit events\n boolean result = customerService.registerCustomer(customer, \"admin\");\n \n // Builder Pattern - Create response\n ApiResponse response;\n if (result) {\n response = new ApiResponse.Builder()\n .success(true)\n .message(\"Customer registered successfully\")\n .data(customer)\n .addMetadata(\"registeredBy\", \"admin\")\n .addMetadata(\"timestamp\", System.currentTimeMillis())\n .build();\n } else {\n response = ApiResponse.error(\"Failed to register customer\");\n }\n \n System.out.println(\"- Integrated operation result: \" + response.toMap());\n \n } catch (Exception e) {\n System.out.println(\"- Error in integrated example: \" + e.getMessage());\n }\n }\n}"}","mcp_server_name":"","mcp_tool_name":""}},{"id":2,"type":0,"content":"Now let me create a comprehensive example showing how to use all the patterns together:
